        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "65ae0604-f622-582b-9411-9f76425318c1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Dain Rauscher Wessels, Berenberg Bank, Royal Bank of Canada\n- People: John G. Taft, Berenberg family\n- Places: Minneapolis, Minnesota, Hamburg\n- Topics: brokerage, investment banking, private banking, acquisitions, company origins\n\nFacts:\n- Berenberg Bank is a Hamburg-based multinational investment banking and private banking company founded by the Belgian-origin Berenberg family in 1590.\n- Dain Rauscher Wessels traced its origins to several smaller regional securities firms founded in the 1920s and 1930s.\n- Dain Rauscher Wessels was a brokerage and investment banking firm based in Minneapolis, Minnesota.\n- John G. Taft worked with Royal Bank of Canada after Royal Bank of Canada acquired Dain Rauscher in 2001.\n- John G. Taft's unit at Dougherty was acquired by Dain Rauscher before Royal Bank of Canada's 2001 acquisition of Dain Rauscher.",
